  "summary": "The code contained a critical security vulnerability due to the use of pickle for untrusted input, which allows for arbitrary code execution. I have replaced pickle with JSON, added input validation, enforced a size limit, and improved code maintainability with type hints and better naming. Overall code health is significantly improved by moving to a secure-by-default serialization approach.",
  "fixed_code": "import base64\nimport json\nfrom flask import Flask, request, abort\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nMAX_SIZE = 1024 * 10  # 10KB limit\n\n@app.route(\"/profile\")\ndef deserialize_data() -> str:\n    '''\n    Get raw_data from request, validate size, decode base64, and parse as JSON.\n    '''\n    raw_data = request.args.get(\"data\")\n    if not raw_data:\n        return \"Missing data\", 400\n    \n    if len(raw_data) > MAX_SIZE:\n        abort(413)\n\n    try:\n        decoded_data = base64.b64decode(raw_data)\n        obj = json.loads(decoded_data)\n        return str(obj)\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError, TypeError):\n        return \"Invalid data format\", 400"
}
